  "count": 101,
  "isIncomplete": false,
  "items": [
    {
      "detail": "pub fn key<T>(default: T) -> Key<T>",
      "documentation": {
        "kind": "markdown",
        "value": "Returns a key whose `get` gives `default` when no value is provided.\nIt must be the whole initializer of a `const`, and every other mention\nof it in an expression is E0080 (D-1045, D-1565, D-1581). The attribute\n`@std_initializer(key_at)` says so to the compiler, which replaces that\none call with a call of `key_at` that also passes the constant's path\nand the text of its value type (D-1572, D-1599). `key` never counts\ntoward satisfying an interface (D-1593). So no program reaches this\nbody, and it panics if a fault of the compiler ever lets one reach it\n(D-1598)."
      },
      "insertTextFormat": 2,
      "kind": 3,
      "label": "key",
